		{"id":"4e937191153a5c90","type":"text","text":"# Gamma\nComputer Screens are usually not linear\n- from old CRT monitors & mimiced on LCD\n- values from framebuffer $(r, g, b)$ mapped to visible intencities $(r^\\gamma , g ^\\gamma, b^\\gamma)$\n$\\gamma \\approx 1.7$\n\n[[HDR encoding]]\n[[Gamma]]","x":-2200,"y":-3320,"width":461,"height":374},
		{"id":"023d0028025ec719","type":"text","text":"# Image Discretization\n[[Aliasing with Fourier]]\n## [[Razterisation]] \n### Sampling:\n- pixel is in or outside the  => but need [[CG Antialiasing]] methods to account for partial coverage\n- Downscale by every 2nd Pixel ![[Pasted image 20260211141306.png]]\n ### Filtering\n- new color average over k-box - [[Box Filter]]\n![[Pasted image 20260211141430.png]]\n","x":-2300,"y":-2020,"width":358,"height":1080},
